# Store all text as LF in the repo so an editor or script that rewrites line
# endings can't turn a 3-line change into a whole-file diff again (upload.css,
# 1 Sep 2026). Windows checkouts still get CRLF via core.autocrlf.
* text=auto
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.webp binary
*.pdf binary
*.xlsx binary

# Vendored third-party builds are stored byte-for-byte as shipped: no line-ending
# translation, and no diffs in review (they are minified, so a diff is noise).
vendor/** -text -diff

# -- GIT LFS ------------------------------------------------------------------
# The Canva source artwork and the photo transport archive go through LFS rather
# than straight into history: ~35MB of binaries in ordinary history is 35MB every
# clone pays for forever, even though none of it is served by the live site. It
# also keeps the door open for an untrimmed export, which GitHub rejects outright
# above its 104,857,600-byte hard limit.
#
# The whole of _source/ is tracked, not just the decks, so anything dropped in
# there later (a re-drawn card, a new head icon) is handled without editing this
# file. Anyone cloning needs git-lfs installed; without it they get small pointer
# files instead of the artwork, which is harmless for the site but confusing if
# you don't know to expect it.
#
# THIS BLOCK WAS LOST ONCE (e8e4bee, 1 Sep 2026) when the line-endings rule
# replaced the file wholesale, and nothing failed until the next big binary was
# added. Add to it; don't rewrite the file over it.
_source/** filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
stylist/photos.zip filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
